---
description:
globs: *.rs
alwaysApply: false
---
Performance is very important.

Rust tests usually go in the bottom of the file in a `tests` mod.

Import common stuff and use the inner name like:
```
use std::time::Instant;

fn foo() {
    let now = Instant::now();
}
``

Inline variables directly in format!-style macros:
`format!("my name is {name}")`

Never use expect or unwrap (outside of tests).
Try to avoid panics, if unavoidable, make it explicit with:
`unwrap_or_else(|_| panic!("..."))`

Public and complex function documentation SHOULD list out individual arguments / return.

Comments go above attributes.